canonical_goals_text:
THE ENHANCED COLLABORATIVE MODEL (ECM) TASK FORCE TO COMBAT HUMAN TRAFFICKING PROGRAM PURPOSE IS TO DEVELOP, EXPAND, OR STRENGTHEN A MULTIDISCIPLINARY APPROACH TO FIGHT HUMAN TRAFFICKING. UNDER THIS PROGRAM, OVC WILL SUPPORT NEW AND PREVIOUSLY FUNDED ECM TASK FORCES IN TWO SEPARATE CATEGORIES. OVERALL ECM PROGRAM OBJECTIVES INCLUDE:
1.	DEVELOP, SUSTAIN, AND STRENGTHEN COORDINATION OF MULTIDISCIPLINARY HUMAN TRAFFICKING TASK FORCE PARTNERSHIPS AND ACTIVITIES; 
2.	IDENTIFY AND SERVE VICTIMS OF ALL TYPES OF HUMAN TRAFFICKING;
3.	IMPLEMENT VICTIM-CENTERED, TRAUMA-INFORMED, AND COLLABORATIVE APPROACHES THROUGH THE DEVELOPMENT AND CONSISTENT IMPLEMENTATION OF TASK FORCE PROTOCOLS AND TRAINING;
4.	ACTIVE INVOLVEMENT OF ALL TASK FORCE PARTNERS IN PLANNING AND EXECUTING PROACTIVE INVESTIGATIONS AND PROSECUTIONS;
5.	INVESTIGATE, REFER, AND PROSECUTE BOTH SEX AND LABOR TRAFFICKING CASES AT THE LOCAL, STATE, TRIBAL, AND FEDERAL LEVELS; 
6.	ASSIST VICTIMS OF SEX TRAFFICKING AND LABOR TRAFFICKING IN ACHIEVING INCREASED SAFETY, INDEPENDENCE, SELF-SUFFICIENCY AND WELL-BEING THROUGH THE PROVISION OF APPROPRIATE SERVICES; AND
7.	CONDUCT DATA COLLECTION AND ONGOING ASSESSMENT ACTIVITIES TO DETERMINE IF THE PROGRAM IS MEETING STATED GOALS AND OBJECTIVES.
